cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Aperture"
abstract: >-
  An interactive explorer and debugger for large language model internals,
  backed by a real GPU. A Python/PyTorch backend loads a Hugging Face
  model's real config and weights (dense or Mixture-of-Experts, optionally
  4-bit/8-bit quantized) and runs actual forward passes and streaming
  generation on the GPU; a React frontend renders its architecture as a
  navigable graph and supports tensor inspection, attention and expert-
  routing views, logit-lens analysis, token attribution, and causal
  interventions.
type: software
authors:
